## KHS Checklist Seed Capture

KHS should request this section from the planner backend, then use it as input for `checklist.md`. This seed is not itself the normalized KHS checklist; KHS/Hermes must validate and normalize it against `registries/phase-contracts.yaml`.

The seed must include explicit skipped-phase reasons for `simple_report`/`simple_command_report`, `investigation`/`research_evidence`, and `docs_only` runs so those task classes do not inherit implementation, enhance-test, optimize, or broad review loops unless classification changes.

Expected seed shape inside `plan.plan_text`:

```markdown
## KHS Checklist Seed

- [ ] phase: plan | evidence: plan.md, checklist.md, acceptance-criteria.md | check: KAH plan gate
- [ ] phase: ralplan | evidence: gjc-ralplan-status.json, gjc-ralplan-artifact.md | check: substantive GJC ralplan candidate evidence before implementation
- [ ] boundary: approval/question evidence | evidence: approval.md, answered-decisions.md, or plan.md#Decision Clarifications when required | check: not a default phase; fail closed if required approval/question evidence is missing
- [ ] phase: implement | evidence: diff.patch, impl-log.md, cli-output.md | check: implementation matches approved scope
```

